Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and inclusion errors.

asr-000503
00:29:39.760 --> 00:29:42.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Bawat piso po ng pondo

asr-000504
00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:43.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ay dapat makarating

asr-000505
00:29:43.460 --> 00:29:44.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: sa totoong nangangailangan

asr-000506
00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:45.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ng walang delay

asr-000507
00:29:45.640 --> 00:29:46.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: at walang pong anomalya.

asr-000508
00:29:48.060 --> 00:29:49.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We are here today

asr-000509
00:29:49.180 --> 00:29:50.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: not to fault-find,

asr-000510
00:29:50.380 --> 00:29:52.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: but to ensure that DSWD

asr-000511
00:29:52.180 --> 00:29:53.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: is given a balanced,

asr-000512
00:29:53.820 --> 00:29:54.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: efficient,

asr-000513
00:29:54.460 --> 00:29:55.600
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and responsive budget.

asr-000514
00:29:56.480 --> 00:29:58.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Gusto pong masiguro

asr-000515
00:29:58.460 --> 00:30:00.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ng representasyong ito

asr-000516
00:30:00.700 --> 00:30:08.980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: na ang bawat piso sa pondo ng DSWD ay magagamit nating tama, mabilis at may tunay na malasakit sa taong bayan.

asr-000517
00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:18.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Let us ensure that the DSWD budget is not only compassionate in purpose but also efficient, accountable and impactful in practice.

asr-000518
00:30:18.400 --> 00:30:28.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Madam Chair, the issues raised by Senator Raffi earlier was discussed already by our Committee on Social Justice and Welfare last Monday

asr-000519
00:30:28.340 --> 00:30:32.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: where we discussed lifetime validity of PWD IDs.

asr-000520
00:30:33.840 --> 00:30:38.880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Maybe the NCDA can reiterate their position regarding these fake IDs.

asr-000521
00:30:39.500 --> 00:30:43.680
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We look forward to a constructive and transparent budget presentation from DSWD.

asr-000522
00:30:44.080 --> 00:30:45.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair.

asr-000523
00:30:46.120 --> 00:30:49.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Maraming salamat din po, Senator and former Secretary Erwin.

asr-000524
00:30:49.720 --> 00:30:50.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you.

asr-000525
00:30:50.420 --> 00:30:54.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, Secretary Rex, you have the floor now to lead the presentation.

asr-000526
00:30:54.680 --> 00:30:58.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Thank you, Madam Chair. Madam Chair, I will go through the top line of the budget.

asr-000527
00:30:58.340 --> 00:31:04.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And then, if you will allow me, I will go straight into the pressing matter on PWD IDs.

asr-000528
00:31:05.180 --> 00:31:05.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, please do.

asr-000529
00:31:05.880 --> 00:31:10.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madam Chairperson and our budget sponsor, Senator Riza Antiveros, honorable members of the Committee,

asr-000530
00:31:10.640 --> 00:31:13.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: co-workers in DSWD, ladies and gentlemen, good afternoon.

asr-000531
00:31:13.560 --> 00:31:18.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The DSWD, including its attached and supervised agencies, is honored to appear before the Senate

asr-000532
00:31:18.740 --> 00:31:22.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: as part of our accountability for the public resources entrusted to us.

asr-000533
00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:27.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In the next slides, we will present our annual budget utilization performance,

asr-000534
00:31:27.580 --> 00:31:33.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the proposed budget for 2027, and the status of major programs implemented by the DSWD.

asr-000535
00:31:34.020 --> 00:31:40.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, the DSWD has a total budget of P240.7 billion under the National Expenditure Program.

asr-000536
00:31:41.240 --> 00:31:46.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Of this amount, P235.7 billion is allocated to the DSWD Office of the Secretary.

asr-000537
00:31:47.200 --> 00:31:50.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For our attached and supervised agencies, the proposed budgets are shown on the screen.

asr-000538
00:31:51.300 --> 00:31:56.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Compared to the 2026 General Appropriations Act, the 2027 NEP for the DSWD,

asr-000539
00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:57.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: including its attached and supervised,

asr-000540
00:31:57.580 --> 00:32:03.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: agencies reflect lower levels, with the exception of NACC and NCSC,

asr-000541
00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:09.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: whose budget increases are under personal services because of new positions created on or filled up.

asr-000542
00:32:10.340 --> 00:32:15.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2025, the DBM released approximately P254 billion to the DSWD,

asr-000543
00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:18.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: both for our agency budget and releases from other fund sources.

asr-000544
00:32:19.300 --> 00:32:25.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are pleased to report that the DSWD achieved a near 100% utilization rate as of September 2026.

asr-000545
00:32:25.380 --> 00:32:27.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2026, the DSWD has so far utilized

asr-000546
00:32:27.580 --> 00:32:33.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 81% of the agency's specific budget of P264.3 billion.

asr-000547
00:32:34.240 --> 00:32:37.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For the Calamity Fund and the Quick Response Fund replenishments,

asr-000548
00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:43.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 83.71% of the P13.7 billion released so far has already been utilized.

asr-000549
00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:48.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Beyond the budget figures, these investments reflect the very essence of DSWD's work,

asr-000550
00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:52.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: investing in human capital development, strengthening community-driven development,

asr-000551
00:32:52.280 --> 00:32:57.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and ensuring a rapid disaster response so that the gains of the development

asr-000552
00:32:57.020 --> 00:32:59.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: are not undone by disasters and other shocks.

asr-000556
00:33:00.180 --> 00:33:04.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: As social risk and vulnerabilities evolve, the DSWD implements innovative flagship programs

asr-000557
00:33:04.780 --> 00:33:10.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and new approaches to address emerging social concerns and response to changing needs of Filipino families.

asr-000558
00:33:11.620 --> 00:33:15.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Walang Gutom addresses food insecurity, Tarabasa supports children's learning,

asr-000559
00:33:15.220 --> 00:33:18.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while providing cash-for-work opportunities for the youth,

asr-000560
00:33:18.360 --> 00:33:20.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and Pag-Abot reaches people in street situations,

asr-000561
00:33:21.320 --> 00:33:23.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: providing immediate food assistance through the Walang Gutom Kitchen,

asr-000562
00:33:23.900 --> 00:33:26.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and connecting them to appropriate social protection services.

asr-000563
00:33:27.580 --> 00:33:35.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Together, these programs invest in people, respond to their specific needs, and help them build more dignified and sustainable lives.

asr-000564
00:33:35.900 --> 00:33:36.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are also?

asr-000564-split-2
00:33:36.480 --> 00:33:47.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sec. Rex, if you could pause for a bit. Tech, pakiayusin natin yung slides ni Secretary. Parang nag-sign out daw. Okay. Salamat. Please proceed, Sec. Rex.

asr-000564-split-3
00:33:47.340 --> 00:33:52.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are also developing targeted responses to prevalent and social welfare concerns.

asr-000565
00:33:52.360 --> 00:33:57.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These include initiatives such as Project Aruga, Protect Teen, and Project Safe for Osaic Victims.

asr-000566
00:33:58.260 --> 00:34:07.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These initiatives address the specific needs of children, adolescents, and families, strengthening our capacity to protect those at risk and deliver appropriate timely support.

asr-000567
00:34:08.080 --> 00:34:17.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: While we continue to innovate and respond to new challenges, we remain fully grounded in our core mandate, delivering regular programs and services that millions of Filipinos depend on.

asr-000568
00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:20.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At the heart of these efforts is our commitment to invest in people.

asr-000569
00:34:21.640 --> 00:34:22.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Helping children.

asr-000570
00:34:22.360 --> 00:34:26.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Helping children grow, families become more self-reliant, and communities move forward.

asr-000571
00:34:27.160 --> 00:34:29.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This is what social protection must deliver.

asr-000572
00:34:29.260 --> 00:34:33.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Immediate support when people need it the most, and sustained opportunities to build a better future.

asr-000573
00:34:34.880 --> 00:34:44.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Let me now turn to our major programs, beginning with Pantawid Pamilang Pilipino Program, or 4Ps, our country's flagship investment in human capital development.

asr-000574
00:34:44.200 --> 00:34:51.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In 2025, we utilized 63.6 billion or 63.7 billion allotment, or 99.83%.

asr-000576
00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:56.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: To pay the conditional cash grants due to the 3.9 million beneficiaries.

asr-000577
00:34:57.200 --> 00:35:07.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2026, our 112.9 billion allotment includes 98.3 billion for grants, with obligation and disbursement progressing according to scheduled payments.

asr-000578
00:35:07.400 --> 00:35:21.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, 99.1 billion budget, including 81.3 billion for grants, will continue to support 3.5 million households, sustaining investments in health, education, and family development,

asr-000579
00:35:21.800 --> 00:35:24.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with focus on poor and near-poor families.

asr-000580
00:35:25.060 --> 00:35:30.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Beyond budget utilization, we measure 4Ps by its results and ensure that our programs are guided by evidence.

asr-000581
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:49.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: From 2022 to July 2026, 1.77 million households graduated to self-sufficiency, 7.24 million children completed primary and secondary education, and 78,886 beneficiaries passed licensure examinations,

asr-000582
00:35:49.740 --> 00:35:52.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: including 259 top-notchers.

asr-000583
00:35:53.280 --> 00:36:03.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under the F1KD First 1,000 Days grant, 83.9% of pregnant beneficiaries nationwide completed the required prenatal visits.

asr-000584
00:36:03.740 --> 00:36:06.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These results are reinforced by independent studies.

asr-000585
00:36:06.940 --> 00:36:17.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The World Bank's 2026 study attributed a 2.2% point reduction in national poverty to 4Ps and estimated a 4.4 cost-benefit ratio.

asr-000586
00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:21.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Brain Trust Study also recognizes the program's educational impact.

asr-000587
00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:23.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in its reach among poor households.

asr-000588
00:36:24.380 --> 00:36:35.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These findings strengthen our commitment to evidence-informed policymaking, continuous program improvement, and ensuring that the public resources deliver measurable results for Filipino families.

asr-000589
00:36:36.220 --> 00:36:44.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under protective services, AICS remains our primary program for individuals and families in crisis, complemented by community-based services for vulnerable sectors.

asr-000590
00:36:44.800 --> 00:36:50.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In 2025, we utilize 100% of the budget, assisting over 9.4 million beneficiaries.

asr-000591
00:36:51.040 --> 00:36:51.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2026,

asr-000592
00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:54.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: utilization has reached almost 92%,

asr-000593
00:36:54.600 --> 00:36:57.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: serving 6.7 million beneficiaries to date.

asr-000594
00:36:58.280 --> 00:37:00.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under the President's Uplift Directive,

asr-000595
00:37:00.220 --> 00:37:03.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we have also assisted 5.8 million beneficiaries

asr-000596
00:37:03.120 --> 00:37:04.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: as of October 14.

asr-000597
00:37:05.280 --> 00:37:08.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, the 33.3 billion,

asr-000598
00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:11.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: including 29.4 billion for subsidies,

asr-000599
00:37:11.620 --> 00:37:13.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: will help individuals and families in crisis

asr-000600
00:37:13.600 --> 00:37:15.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: meet urgent needs,

asr-000601
00:37:15.640 --> 00:37:16.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: access essential services,

asr-000602
00:37:16.940 --> 00:37:19.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and recover from financial and personal hardships.

asr-000603
00:37:19.560 --> 00:37:21.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: However, additional resources

asr-000604
00:37:21.100 --> 00:37:22.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: may be needed to keep pace

asr-000605
00:37:22.560 --> 00:37:23.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with the growing demand

asr-000606
00:37:23.380 --> 00:37:24.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and sustain these outcomes.

asr-000607
00:37:25.320 --> 00:37:25.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Your Honors,

asr-000608
00:37:25.880 --> 00:37:27.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: AICS is evolving into an instrument

asr-000609
00:37:27.940 --> 00:37:30.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for adaptive and shock-responsive social protection.

asr-000610
00:37:31.660 --> 00:37:33.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under the President's Uplift Initiative,

asr-000611
00:37:33.640 --> 00:37:35.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we provided 5,000 cash assistance

asr-000612
00:37:35.960 --> 00:37:39.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to 1.839 million transport workers.

asr-000613
00:37:40.140 --> 00:37:43.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: A rapid SWS assessment

asr-000614
00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:47.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: found that 96% considered the grant crucial

asr-000615
00:37:47.380 --> 00:37:48.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to keeping them on the road,

asr-000616
00:37:48.840 --> 00:37:51.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while 80% use it for food,

asr-000617
00:37:51.100 --> 00:37:53.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while we also provided top-up support

asr-000618
00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:55.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for existing beneficiaries

asr-000619
00:37:55.100 --> 00:37:57.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and extended aid to vulnerable households

asr-000620
00:37:57.620 --> 00:37:59.320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: identified through CBMS data.

asr-000621
00:37:59.860 --> 00:38:02.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This demonstrates how AICS can scale up support

asr-000622
00:38:02.440 --> 00:38:05.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and reach families vulnerable to economic shocks

asr-000623
00:38:05.100 --> 00:38:06.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: when they need it the most.

asr-000624
00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:09.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Another key investment is the social protection pension

asr-000625
00:38:09.700 --> 00:38:12.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for indigent senior citizens,

asr-000626
00:38:12.660 --> 00:38:15.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: providing vital income support to our older persons.

asr-000627
00:38:16.100 --> 00:38:19.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In 2025, we serve 4.11 million beneficiaries.

asr-000628
00:38:19.480 --> 00:38:20.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2026,

asr-000629
00:38:21.100 --> 00:38:23.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: utilization is at 88%

asr-000630
00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:24.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: as we enroll new beneficiaries

asr-000631
00:38:24.900 --> 00:38:27.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with 51 billion available to expand coverage.

asr-000632
00:38:27.900 --> 00:38:29.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027,

asr-000633
00:38:29.480 --> 00:38:34.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the 51.6 billion budget allots 50 billion for subsidies.

asr-000634
00:38:34.300 --> 00:38:37.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We would like to flag that based on CBMS data,

asr-000635
00:38:37.140 --> 00:38:41.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: at least 550,000 older seniors,

asr-000636
00:38:41.020 --> 00:38:43.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: older persons remain unserved

asr-000637
00:38:43.300 --> 00:38:45.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and we hope to extend social pension

asr-000638
00:38:45.220 --> 00:38:46.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to these senior citizens.

asr-000639
00:38:46.940 --> 00:38:47.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For social pension,

asr-000640
00:38:47.860 --> 00:38:49.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we are making implementation simpler,

asr-000641
00:38:49.580 --> 00:38:50.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: fairer, and more responsive,

asr-000642
00:38:50.900 --> 00:38:53.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in support of the progressive realization

asr-000643
00:38:53.420 --> 00:38:55.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of universal social pension.

asr-000644
00:38:55.420 --> 00:38:57.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: First, we removed the requirement

asr-000645
00:38:57.860 --> 00:39:02.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to provide frailty or sickliness eligibility.

asr-000646
00:39:02.220 --> 00:39:04.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Eligibility is now based on age,

asr-000647
00:39:04.620 --> 00:39:07.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with enrollment prioritized by age.

asr-000648
00:39:07.260 --> 00:39:10.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Second, we shifted to data-driven targeting

asr-000649
00:39:10.260 --> 00:39:11.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: using CBMS data,

asr-000650
00:39:11.740 --> 00:39:15.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: cross-checked with SSS, GSIS, and PVOW,

asr-000651
00:39:15.260 --> 00:39:18.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to ensure applicants are not active pensioners.

asr-000652
00:39:18.140 --> 00:39:20.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: To reach those who may be missed

asr-000653
00:39:20.140 --> 00:39:20.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: by the field

asr-000654
00:39:20.860 --> 00:39:23.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or those who may not be included in the program,

asr-000655
00:39:23.140 --> 00:39:25.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we also allowed applications

asr-000656
00:39:25.660 --> 00:39:29.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and LGU referrals for persons aged 70 and above,

asr-000657
00:39:29.780 --> 00:39:33.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: subject to validation with DSA registry data.

asr-000658
00:39:33.540 --> 00:39:37.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Finally, we are advancing the silver economy across ASEAN,

asr-000659
00:39:37.220 --> 00:39:38.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: recognizing older persons

asr-000660
00:39:38.780 --> 00:39:41.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: not only as beneficiaries to social protection,

asr-000661
00:39:41.380 --> 00:39:44.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: but also as contributors to communities and the economy.

asr-000662
00:39:44.420 --> 00:39:47.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The supplementary feeding program provides support,

asr-000663
00:39:47.140 --> 00:39:48.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: supports the nutrition needs of children

asr-000664
00:39:48.980 --> 00:39:50.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in child development centers,

asr-000665
00:39:50.420 --> 00:39:52.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and supervised neighborhood place.

asr-000666
00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:55.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, the 6.4 billion budget

asr-000667
00:39:55.620 --> 00:39:59.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: will provide supplementary meals to 1.899 million children,

asr-000668
00:39:59.020 --> 00:40:03.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: sustaining coverage at the first fiscal year 2026 target.

asr-000669
00:40:03.660 --> 00:40:07.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The lower allocation reflects a shorter feeding period

asr-000670
00:40:07.140 --> 00:40:11.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of 120 days compared with 180 days in 2026,

asr-000671
00:40:11.660 --> 00:40:14.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: not a reduction of children served.

asr-000672
00:40:14.780 --> 00:40:18.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Social protection must create pathways to self-reliance.

asr-000673
00:40:18.260 --> 00:40:19.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Through the Sustainable Livelihood program,

asr-000674
00:40:19.540 --> 00:40:20.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we help families in rural areas,

asr-000675
00:40:20.260 --> 00:40:23.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: families generate income and achieve economic independence.

asr-000676
00:40:23.280 --> 00:40:29.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In 2025, SLP assisted 275,478 households exceeding its target

asr-000677
00:40:29.920 --> 00:40:36.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with 100% of its 6.2 allocation obligated as of September 2026.

asr-000678
00:40:37.160 --> 00:40:40.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 238,233 households have been assisted.

asr-000679
00:40:40.840 --> 00:40:47.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, the 5.1 billion budget will support 251,449 households

asr-000680
00:40:47.300 --> 00:40:50.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in developing sustainable livelihoods, generating income,

asr-000681
00:40:50.800 --> 00:40:53.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and achieving greater economic self-reliance.

asr-000682
00:40:53.600 --> 00:40:55.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Given the program's performance and reach,

asr-000683
00:40:55.440 --> 00:40:58.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: additional funding may be needed to extend these opportunities to more families.

asr-000684
00:40:59.600 --> 00:41:03.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We have revamped SLP to move beyond one-time assistance

asr-000685
00:41:03.200 --> 00:41:06.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: towards sustainable enterprise development.

asr-000686
00:41:07.320 --> 00:41:11.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Through Pag-CBOL, we provide long-term support and sustainability plans

asr-000687
00:41:11.280 --> 00:41:14.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to help livelihood grow into viable sources of income.

asr-000688
00:41:14.620 --> 00:41:16.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We also strengthen market linkages

asr-000689
00:41:16.740 --> 00:41:20.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and open new sales channels including digital platforms like TikTok.

asr-000690
00:41:20.880 --> 00:41:24.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Our goal is clear, invest in livelihoods that can grow, compete,

asr-000691
00:41:24.680 --> 00:41:26.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and provide sustainable income for families.

asr-000692
00:41:26.900 --> 00:41:30.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: A consistent part of our mandate is to provide residential and center-based services

asr-000693
00:41:30.740 --> 00:41:34.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for individuals who require more intensive and sustained care.

asr-000694
00:41:34.460 --> 00:41:37.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These include children, older persons, persons with disabilities,

asr-000695
00:41:37.640 --> 00:41:41.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and other individuals whose circumstances require specific intervention.

asr-000696
00:41:41.360 --> 00:41:46.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2025, we serve 9,620 clients,

asr-000697
00:41:46.180 --> 00:41:49.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: exceeding the target by 11.34%,

asr-000698
00:41:49.560 --> 00:41:56.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while in 2026, 8,674 clients have already been served as of this reporting period.

asr-000699
00:41:57.580 --> 00:42:03.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, the 3.3 billion budget will provide specialized care and support

asr-000700
00:42:03.300 --> 00:42:08.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to 8,640 clients, helping meet their needs and improve their well-being.

asr-000701
00:42:08.820 --> 00:42:13.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Our challenge is to ensure that our 77 residential and center-based facilities

asr-000702
00:42:13.700 --> 00:42:16.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: remain safe, appropriate, accessible, and sustainable.

asr-000703
00:42:16.180 --> 00:42:19.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are also capable of delivering quality social welfare services.

asr-000704
00:42:19.900 --> 00:42:23.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It is for this reason that we are proposing P286.1 million

asr-000705
00:42:23.540 --> 00:42:27.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for power system rehabilitation of our care facilities.

asr-000706
00:42:27.680 --> 00:42:31.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: To address overcapacity, we are also seeking an additional P204 million

asr-000707
00:42:31.520 --> 00:42:36.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for cost-of-care subsidies to qualified private social welfare agencies,

asr-000708
00:42:36.820 --> 00:42:40.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 50 of which have already been operating beyond their bed capacity.

asr-000709
00:42:41.360 --> 00:42:43.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These investments will improve care facilities

asr-000710
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:46.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and expand our capacity to serve vulnerable clients.

asr-000711
00:42:46.180 --> 00:42:51.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: On disaster response, the QRS allows DSWD to provide timely assistance

asr-000712
00:42:51.260 --> 00:42:53.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: before, during, and after emergencies,

asr-000713
00:42:53.920 --> 00:42:56.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ensuring that affected families feel the government's presence

asr-000714
00:42:56.500 --> 00:42:57.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: when they need it the most.

asr-000715
00:42:58.180 --> 00:43:01.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We fully utilize the 2025 allotment and replenishment.

asr-000716
00:43:02.880 --> 00:43:07.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2026, we have utilized 14.3 billion of the 16.7 billion release.

asr-000717
00:43:08.700 --> 00:43:12.320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Our strategy is always present where disasters strike

asr-000718
00:43:12.320 --> 00:43:14.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with relief goods ready for immediate deployment.

asr-000719
00:43:14.780 --> 00:43:18.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We have 1,048 warehouses nationwide

asr-000720
00:43:18.360 --> 00:43:24.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with 4.4 million family food packs in stock as of September 30, 2026.

asr-000721
00:43:24.620 --> 00:43:28.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Our modernized facilities can produce up to 63,000 food packs per shift

asr-000722
00:43:28.620 --> 00:43:32.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with 7.2 million food packs produced in 2025.

asr-000723
00:43:33.080 --> 00:43:36.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We also provide emergency cash transfers and cash for work in 2025.

asr-000724
00:43:37.360 --> 00:43:41.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 1.3 million families benefited from or receive help

asr-000725
00:43:41.220 --> 00:43:43.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to meet urgent needs and begin recovery.

asr-000726
00:43:43.160 --> 00:43:44.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027,

asr-000727
00:43:44.780 --> 00:43:48.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the 1.9 billion budget for disaster response and rehabilitation

asr-000728
00:43:48.680 --> 00:43:51.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: will continue the implementation of LAWA and BINHI,

asr-000729
00:43:52.180 --> 00:43:56.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: which provides cash support for temporary employment

asr-000730
00:43:56.360 --> 00:43:59.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and skills training to poor and disadvantaged families

asr-000731
00:43:59.760 --> 00:44:03.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: vulnerable to climate hazards, including El Ni?o-induced drought.

asr-000732
00:44:04.060 --> 00:44:06.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Drought requires a whole-of-government approach.

asr-000733
00:44:06.760 --> 00:44:09.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: DSWD provides social protection and humanitarian assistance

asr-000734
00:44:09.460 --> 00:44:13.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to meet urgent needs, protect food security and help affected families

asr-000735
00:44:13.020 --> 00:44:14.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: recover and restore their livelihoods.

asr-000736
00:44:14.780 --> 00:44:18.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This includes complementing the efforts of partner agencies and LGUs.

asr-000737
00:44:19.460 --> 00:44:22.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This slide will show practical components of LAWA and BINHI,

asr-000738
00:44:22.700 --> 00:44:25.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: protecting water access, sustaining food production,

asr-000739
00:44:25.800 --> 00:44:27.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and strengthening livelihoods.

asr-000740
00:44:27.580 --> 00:44:31.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The approach is intended to help communities address immediate effects of El Nino

asr-000741
00:44:31.020 --> 00:44:33.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while building capacity to withstand future shocks.

asr-000742
00:44:34.420 --> 00:44:38.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The department's role is complemented by coordination with relevant partners,

asr-000743
00:44:38.380 --> 00:44:41.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: particularly for technical support and provision of agriculture inputs

asr-000744
00:44:41.980 --> 00:44:43.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and other sector-driven assistance.

asr-000745
00:44:43.900 --> 00:44:44.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In addition,

asr-000746
00:44:44.780 --> 00:44:49.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the department also uses its quick response fund for emergency cash transfer.

asr-000747
00:44:49.340 --> 00:44:53.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It provides temporary unconditional cash support to individuals and families

asr-000748
00:44:53.180 --> 00:44:56.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: affected by crises, disaster, and economic shocks.

asr-000749
00:44:56.600 --> 00:44:59.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This slide presents assistance for affected

asr-000750
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: farmers in Regions 3 and 5

asr-000751
00:45:02.160 --> 00:45:04.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: including 77,260

asr-000752
00:45:04.860 --> 00:45:06.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: farmers in Region 3

asr-000753
00:45:06.200 --> 00:45:09.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and 26,041

asr-000754
00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:10.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in Region 5.

asr-000755
00:45:10.980 --> 00:45:12.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The grant is calculated

