DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It will take full effect by December.

asr-002908
02:08:40.740 --> 02:08:42.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Anong kakaiba sa system na to?

asr-002909
02:08:42.180 --> 02:08:43.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's fully integrated.

asr-002910
02:08:43.160 --> 02:08:46.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So from the time you register as a beneficiary all the way to payout,

asr-002911
02:08:46.860 --> 02:08:49.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: wala na hong download, encode, upload, wala na hong ganon.

asr-002912
02:08:50.140 --> 02:08:52.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we've armed our 14...

asr-002913
02:08:52.280 --> 02:09:00.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 15,000 na mga links, case managers, with an iPad, with a tablet, and a laptop.

asr-002914
02:09:00.380 --> 02:09:06.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi nga, there's no point in buying a new system if you don't arm them with hardware.

asr-002915
02:09:06.680 --> 02:09:07.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So kompleto na ho sila.

asr-002916
02:09:08.580 --> 02:09:13.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So the beauty of that is, kung dati-rati nag-aantay ho ang ating mga grantees

asr-002917
02:09:13.560 --> 02:09:16.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ng almost 60 days to 75 days to get their grants,

asr-002918
02:09:16.960 --> 02:09:21.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in the new system, makukuha na nila yung health grant nila at rise subsidy nila

asr-002919
02:09:21.460 --> 02:09:24.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: within the same month, or 45 days, within 45 days.

asr-002920
02:09:25.180 --> 02:09:28.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, also, meron ho itong collateral benefits sa DepEd.

asr-002921
02:09:29.160 --> 02:09:31.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The new system is now self-contained.

asr-002922
02:09:31.980 --> 02:09:35.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi dati, kinukomplain ng DepEd na yung mga guro nila ang gumagawa ng compliance,

asr-002923
02:09:36.240 --> 02:09:39.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kaya napaka-volumous nung report doon sa EDUC grant.

asr-002924
02:09:39.620 --> 02:09:41.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So nababawasan yung oras nila magturo.

asr-002925
02:09:41.960 --> 02:09:45.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So by the end of the year, it will be beneficiaries-driven na.

asr-002926
02:09:45.940 --> 02:09:48.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi na kami aasa sa mga guro natin na gumawa ng report,

asr-002927
02:09:48.920 --> 02:09:50.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kundi yung report card na mismo ng mga bata,

asr-002928
02:09:51.460 --> 02:09:54.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ng ating mga magulang, during the family development session,

asr-002929
02:09:55.180 --> 02:09:58.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: scan, update the record, you get your education grant.

asr-002930
02:09:58.620 --> 02:09:59.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sa health grant, ganun din.

asr-002931
02:09:59.860 --> 02:10:04.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: They will have their own booklets na hindi na kami aasa sa mga DOH barangay doctors

asr-002932
02:10:04.580 --> 02:10:06.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kasi ang dami na nilang ginagawa.

asr-002933
02:10:06.240 --> 02:10:08.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So the system is self-contained and it's more efficient.

asr-002934
02:10:09.480 --> 02:10:16.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, we are also coming up with a support program for the child-monitored children.

asr-002935
02:10:16.760 --> 02:10:19.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nakita natin sa datos, and alam ko, alam to ng Senate President,

asr-002936
02:10:19.740 --> 02:10:25.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: pagdating sa comparison ng studies between four-piece and non-four-piece sa basic ed,

asr-002937
02:10:26.480 --> 02:10:28.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: pantay, near universal.

asr-002938
02:10:28.680 --> 02:10:30.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pagdating sa secondary ed, education,

asr-002939
02:10:31.360 --> 02:10:35.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the four-piece beneficiaries does slightly better than non-four-piece beneficiaries,

asr-002940
02:10:36.400 --> 02:10:39.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: pero sabay rin silang bumabagsak pagdating sa tertiary education.

asr-002941
02:10:40.240 --> 02:10:45.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ang maganda hong nagpapasalamat kami dahil sa new tertiary amendments to the TES,

asr-002942
02:10:45.100 --> 02:10:49.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: e ngayon talagang categorical na sinabi na four-piece not listed.

asr-002943
02:10:49.740 --> 02:10:56.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So talagang, we've already embarked on a massive education campaign to our beneficiaries to avail of this service.

asr-002944
02:10:56.640 --> 02:11:00.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero during my talks with the beneficiaries, marami sa kanila pa rin ang sinasabi,

asr-002945
02:11:00.880 --> 02:11:03.320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: yung cost of going to school is the problem.

asr-002946
02:11:03.780 --> 02:11:07.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi marami sa kanila na sa mga bundok, so they have to, bundok at isla,

asr-002947
02:11:07.840 --> 02:11:10.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or geographically isolated and disadvantaged area,

asr-002948
02:11:10.580 --> 02:11:15.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: luluwa sila sa mga capital or city centers para mag-dorm, para mag-aral.

asr-002949
02:11:15.160 --> 02:11:19.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So the program has a distinct feature.

asr-002950
02:11:19.740 --> 02:11:23.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's called the Enhanced Support Service Intervention.

asr-002951
02:11:23.440 --> 02:11:26.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nung dumating ako nandiyan na ho yan, it's enshrined in the guideline.

asr-002952
02:11:26.540 --> 02:11:30.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madati, yung pondo na yun, it's part of the budget already, we're not going to ask for more.

asr-002953
02:11:30.880 --> 02:11:34.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ginagamit lang yan sa a varied myriad of things.

asr-002954
02:11:34.520 --> 02:11:38.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: May livelihood, okay naman, merong support, other support.

asr-002955
02:11:38.180 --> 02:11:42.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now we've converted it and we're launching it come December.

asr-002956
02:11:42.020 --> 02:11:48.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's called the Tuloy Program, meaning Tuloy Kolehyo, Tuloy Aral at Tuloy Trabaho.

asr-002957
02:11:48.220 --> 02:11:56.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we, consulting with development experts, we will now come up with yung mga monitored children.

asr-002958
02:11:56.220 --> 02:12:04.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: If they can show that nag-enroll sila, then we will give them a one-time 10,000 grant na 10,000 assistance para mag-tuloy ng kolehyo.

asr-002959
02:12:04.940 --> 02:12:11.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, succeedingly, if they continue to stay in college, then they can show the attendance through the requirements we'll ask for.

asr-002960
02:12:11.800 --> 02:12:17.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tuloy Aral naman, they get additional 5,000 that they can use together with the allowance they get from TES

asr-002961
02:12:17.020 --> 02:12:18.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to support

asr-002963
02:12:18.220 --> 02:12:19.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: their course of studying.

asr-002964
02:12:20.420 --> 02:12:31.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And last, Tuloy Trabaho is when they do graduate out of college, we give them another one-time grant na 10,000 so that they can embark on career,

asr-002965
02:12:32.280 --> 02:12:35.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: meaning to get the requirements, whatever pre-employment requirements they need.

asr-002966
02:12:36.360 --> 02:12:41.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, in-enhance lang namin yung program to make sure that we lengthen the horizon at matuloy talaga yung pag-aaral nila.

asr-002967
02:12:42.140 --> 02:12:48.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, I know I've said a lot, but those are the program enhancements, but if you're looking for the impacts, we can flash

asr-002968
02:12:48.020 --> 02:12:49.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: on the screen the impacts.

asr-002969
02:12:51.020 --> 02:12:51.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kanina ko ba sinabi?

asr-002970
02:12:52.660 --> 02:12:53.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Who's the impacts?

asr-002971
02:12:58.940 --> 02:12:59.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Akin yung impact.

asr-002972
02:13:01.620 --> 02:13:03.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kanina pala sinabi, hindi mo nalimot.

asr-002973
02:13:04.740 --> 02:13:07.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ito ba yung page 9 nyo sa CREX?

asr-002974
02:13:07.120 --> 02:13:07.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay, there we are.

asr-002975
02:13:07.900 --> 02:13:14.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, after 18 years, very, very clear na ho yung mga impacts, numerous impact assessments have been done.

asr-002976
02:13:14.940 --> 02:13:17.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: First things first, the World Bank has already said,

asr-002977
02:13:17.580 --> 02:13:24.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na number one, the four-piece program can be attributed to 2.2% poverty reduction.

asr-002978
02:13:25.040 --> 02:13:31.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Its cost per, its rate of return is also one of the better ones for the government.

asr-002979
02:13:31.960 --> 02:13:32.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ano saan ba yan?

asr-002980
02:13:33.040 --> 02:13:33.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes, sir.

asr-002981
02:13:34.140 --> 02:13:34.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi ko nga makita

asr-002982
02:13:34.860 --> 02:13:36.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Which page?

asr-002983
02:13:36.260 --> 02:13:37.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ...

asr-002984
02:13:37.260 --> 02:13:37.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ...

asr-002985
02:13:39.200 --> 02:13:40.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nasaan ito ba?

asr-002986
02:13:40.500 --> 02:13:41.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ...

asr-002987
02:13:42.300 --> 02:13:45.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, again, the rate of return is one of the better ones.

asr-002988
02:13:45.680 --> 02:13:46.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And then,

asr-002989
02:13:47.580 --> 02:13:50.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, these are independent assessments done by so many groups.

asr-002990
02:13:51.200 --> 02:13:55.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Also, there's a World Bank study that is already published that says,

asr-002991
02:13:55.380 --> 02:14:02.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: number one, our four-piece children compared to our non-four-piece children stay in school longer by almost

asr-002992
02:14:02.280 --> 02:14:13.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 53% of our former youth beneficiaries earn the bachelor's degree versus 31% for non-beneficiaries.

asr-002993
02:14:13.740 --> 02:14:17.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, that means they're staying in school and completing their college education.

asr-002994
02:14:17.580 --> 02:14:27.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Then, 44% of those na beneficiaries namin end up with permanent jobs, nearly double the non-four-piece na beneficiaries.

asr-002995
02:14:28.020 --> 02:14:30.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 25% lang yun, kami 44%.

asr-002996
02:14:30.460 --> 02:14:36.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, meaning nakakapagtrabaho sila, so natutuloy na yung pagputol ng intergenerational poverty.

asr-002997
02:14:36.640 --> 02:14:44.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And last, they also cited the 55% of our young women, former young four-piece beneficiaries,

asr-002998
02:14:44.640 --> 02:14:45.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: achieve permanent employment compared to 33%.

asr-002999
02:14:47.580 --> 02:14:52.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, nakikita na po natin yung fruition ng programa.

asr-003000
02:14:52.720 --> 02:14:59.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Although early, pero 18 years later, nasusukat na natin concretely na nabibreak yung intergenerational poverty.

asr-003001
02:15:00.240 --> 02:15:08.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Beyond the numbers that I showed kanina, how many thousands graduated, these numbers speak for the program's fruition of breaking intergenerational poverty.

asr-003002
02:15:09.340 --> 02:15:24.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Also, in the PSA study, sorry, not the PSA study, the latest FIES of PSA, they cited five things why poverty also went down to 9%.

asr-003003
02:15:24.480 --> 02:15:33.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: First, in a household, you would get foreign remittance, so yung mga OFW nila nakamag-anak, entrepreneurship, nakapaghanap ng hanap buhay,

asr-003004
02:15:35.380 --> 02:15:42.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the controlled prices dahil inflation was low, but one of the reasons they also cited is cash transfers.

asr-003005
02:15:43.640 --> 02:15:49.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And a big chunk of that in protecting the households and pulling them out of poverty was cash transfer.

asr-003006
02:15:49.700 --> 02:15:53.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And attributable yan to a big chunk sa 4Ps.

asr-003007
02:15:54.480 --> 02:15:59.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you for those answers.

asr-003008
02:16:01.580 --> 02:16:08.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, itong program na ito, ang isang programa na pag bumaba ba yung budget, natutuwa ko eh.

asr-003009
02:16:08.720 --> 02:16:13.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil alam natin na bumaba ba yung bilang ng mahihirap sa ating bansa.

asr-003010
02:16:13.800 --> 02:16:20.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Of course, malayo pa tayo with 3.5 million poorest of the poor family.

asr-003011
02:16:20.780 --> 02:16:24.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But tutuwa ko dahil 1.7 million ang...

asr-003012
02:16:24.480 --> 02:16:28.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: na ilabas natin sa poorest of the poor category.

asr-003013
02:16:28.920 --> 02:16:33.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ngayon, my next question is, how do we continue the gains?

asr-003014
02:16:35.240 --> 02:16:38.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: This is related to what I said earlier, which is El Nino.

asr-003015
02:16:39.720 --> 02:16:46.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And also, yung last PSA poverty survey was 2025.

asr-003016
02:16:47.200 --> 02:16:48.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Wala pang gera ng era nun.

asr-003017
02:16:49.380 --> 02:16:50.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Wala pa tayong El Nino.

asr-003018
02:16:51.140 --> 02:16:53.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Wala pa tayong 7.5 inflation.

asr-003019
02:16:54.480 --> 02:16:58.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 2025, actually, mababa ang inflation natin at that time.

asr-003020
02:16:58.280 --> 02:17:09.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Inflation is a, I would call it, is a poverty, it can cause poverty in our country.

asr-003021
02:17:09.800 --> 02:17:21.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, how do we maintain yung pababa na trajectory ng poverty reduction natin?

asr-003022
02:17:21.600 --> 02:17:23.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll start off with El Nino.

asr-003023
02:17:24.480 --> 02:17:31.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then, I also want to understand anong ginagawa ng department to prepare for this El Nino.

asr-003024
02:17:31.700 --> 02:17:35.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kanina sinabi ni Secretary na they're looking at...

asr-003025
02:17:35.700 --> 02:17:40.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Secretary Kiko Laurela, they're looking at...

asr-003026
02:17:44.360 --> 02:17:52.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: close to 350,000 affected farmers.

asr-003027
02:17:52.960 --> 02:17:53.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: No?

asr-003028
02:17:53.160 --> 02:17:53.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, medyo...

asr-003029
02:17:54.480 --> 02:17:55.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Malaki-laki yun.

asr-003030
02:18:00.920 --> 02:18:03.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And, of course, itong affected farmers,

asr-003031
02:18:04.200 --> 02:18:07.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: mawawalan sila ng trabaho, mawawalan sila ng livelihood.

asr-003032
02:18:07.260 --> 02:18:08.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, how are we preparing for that?

asr-003033
02:18:09.640 --> 02:18:13.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Secrex, bago kayo sumagot, gusto lang i-acknowledge ng chair,

asr-003034
02:18:13.420 --> 02:18:17.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung presensya ng aming Finance Committee Chair, Senator JV.

asr-003035
02:18:18.420 --> 02:18:20.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat sa pagdalo ninyo.

asr-003036
02:18:20.060 --> 02:18:22.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At presensya din ni Senator Bong Go.

asr-003037
02:18:23.240 --> 02:18:24.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat kayo, Senator.

asr-003038
02:18:24.320 --> 02:18:26.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you, Senator Bong, for joining us.

asr-003039
02:18:26.760 --> 02:18:32.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: After yung itong first round ni SP, tanongin ko kayo dalawa kung gusto nyo mag-opening remarks.

asr-003040
02:18:33.660 --> 02:18:34.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: When the...

asr-003041
02:18:35.020 --> 02:18:41.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang sabi pala ni Secretary Kiko Laurela is 4 million farmers can be affected at the worst case scenario.

asr-003042
02:18:42.600 --> 02:18:46.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we have 10 million workers in the agriculture industry.

asr-003043
02:18:47.180 --> 02:18:48.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil nga, iba, drought eh.

asr-003044
02:18:48.960 --> 02:18:51.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Wala silang pwedeng pagtaniman.

asr-003045
02:18:53.220 --> 02:18:53.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At...

asr-003046
02:18:53.460 --> 02:18:58.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Talagang magkakaroon tayo ng widespread unemployment kung at the worst case scenario.

asr-003047
02:18:59.100 --> 02:19:00.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, two questions.

asr-003048
02:19:01.020 --> 02:19:03.760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: One is, how do we prevent El Nino?

asr-003049
02:19:04.420 --> 02:19:08.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Or how do we mitigate El Nino in terms of poverty reduction?

asr-003050
02:19:08.160 --> 02:19:11.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And how are we addressing El Nino this coming next few months?

asr-003051
02:19:12.700 --> 02:19:15.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madam Sir, bago ko siguro masagot yung El Nino,

asr-003052
02:19:15.120 --> 02:19:19.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: lagay ko muna sa konteksto nung responde namin sa energy emergency.

asr-003053
02:19:19.460 --> 02:19:23.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi yung energy emergency was already detrimental or nanganib na ho sila noon.

asr-003054
02:19:23.460 --> 02:19:27.320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, when I say sila, yung mga near poor and poor families ho natin,

asr-003055
02:19:27.400 --> 02:19:29.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kasama yung mga 4Ps ho natin doon.

asr-003056
02:19:30.080 --> 02:19:33.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We were working closely with the PEDS or one of their fellows,

asr-003057
02:19:33.580 --> 02:19:36.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: si Professor Toots Albert, in designing the uplift assistance.

asr-003058
02:19:37.320 --> 02:19:42.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This comes into play kasi we were looking at the diminished na spending power nila

asr-003059
02:19:42.000 --> 02:19:45.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of almost around 1,200 to 1,500 pesos.

asr-003060
02:19:45.880 --> 02:19:50.320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Doon namin na-draw yung 2,000 pesos monthly na ipinamahagi sa kanila.

asr-003061
02:19:50.320 --> 02:19:52.320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, we embarked on a...

asr-003062
02:19:52.340 --> 02:19:53.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tawag namin,

asr-003063
02:19:53.240 --> 02:19:57.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This is an EVH, Emergency Scheme, Vertical Expansion or Horizontal Expansion.

asr-003064
02:19:58.340 --> 02:20:01.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ito ho yung rasyonale ng design ng uplift assistance.

asr-003065
02:20:01.260 --> 02:20:03.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's why una, may Group 1 tayo.

asr-003066
02:20:03.460 --> 02:20:10.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nakatanggap ang ating mga 4Ps beneficiaries ng one-time top-up na 2,000 pesos last July or August.

asr-003067
02:20:11.220 --> 02:20:17.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The second one was Group 2, meaning yung mga near poor or poor na hindi ho bahagi ng 4Ps

asr-003068
02:20:17.780 --> 02:20:19.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: dahil they did not meet the conditionalities.

asr-003069
02:20:19.860 --> 02:20:22.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: There are around 2.5 million households doon.

asr-003070
02:20:23.000 --> 02:20:23.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yun ho.

asr-003071
02:20:23.240 --> 02:20:28.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nakakatanggap yun at patuloy nakakatanggap ng 2,000 pesos since July all the way to December.

asr-003072
02:20:28.660 --> 02:20:31.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sa aming pag-uusap sa uplift committee at sa direktiba ng ating Pangulo,

asr-003073
02:20:31.800 --> 02:20:35.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we are playing it close to the ground na kung humaba yung energy emergency,

asr-003074
02:20:35.700 --> 02:20:36.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: e maaring humaba rin to.

asr-003075
02:20:37.260 --> 02:20:41.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, for now, ang design niya is still December, but we will look at the situation

asr-003076
02:20:41.800 --> 02:20:45.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and if we're warranted, sinabi naman ang ating Pangulo that we can extend this.

asr-003077
02:20:45.380 --> 02:20:49.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, Group 3 is yung low-wage SSS earners.

asr-003078
02:20:50.220 --> 02:20:52.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's 1.5 million families naman.

asr-003079
02:20:53.240 --> 02:20:54.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Individuals or household.

asr-003080
02:20:54.860 --> 02:21:00.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yan naman ho, kinonsider namin sila na vulnerable because their monthly salary credits only amounts to 20,000.

asr-003081
02:21:01.220 --> 02:21:07.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In fact, later on, in-expand pa namin all the way to mas mababa na 10,000 pesos monthly salary credit.

asr-003082
02:21:07.920 --> 02:21:11.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, Madam Chair, I spoke about this kasi yung target, etong mga grupo na to,

asr-003083
02:21:12.220 --> 02:21:15.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: sigurado ko sila rin yung maapektuhan ng Elminio.

asr-003084
02:21:15.160 --> 02:21:22.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, right now, we gave protection to 7.5 million families.

asr-003085
02:21:22.580 --> 02:21:27.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: A lot of these families will be the same families that will be severely affected by the Elminio drought.

asr-003086
02:21:28.320 --> 02:21:33.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Marami, 70% to 85% of our four-piece beneficiaries are farmers.

asr-003087
02:21:34.220 --> 02:21:39.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In fact, a big chunk of Group 2, Group 1, are not in the urban areas.

asr-003088
02:21:39.720 --> 02:21:42.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: They're in the municipalities or rural areas.

asr-003089
02:21:42.660 --> 02:21:44.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nakikita namin yan when we do the payouts.

asr-003090
02:21:45.600 --> 02:21:49.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, moving forward, I want to show our slide.

asr-003091
02:21:49.000 --> 02:21:50.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meron ba tayong presentation ng El Niño?

asr-003092
02:21:51.260 --> 02:21:51.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ...

asr-003093
02:21:51.660 --> 02:21:54.820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, the El Niño preparations of the department.

asr-003094
02:21:56.140 --> 02:22:01.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ito po, when I got to the department, and alam ko nire-reform rin ito ni Sen. Erwin noon, hindi lang yan natapos.

asr-003095
02:22:02.340 --> 02:22:09.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We have a line item called the Disaster Resilience Response Rehabilitation Program, DRRP.

asr-003096
02:22:09.940 --> 02:22:12.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That's a 1.1 billion expenditure in our books.

asr-003097
02:22:13.480 --> 02:22:18.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, nung nadatna namin yan, that's a cash-for-work program na yung work program was very loose

asr-003098
02:22:18.100 --> 02:22:20.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in the sense na iba-iba yung pinagagawa sa kanila.

asr-003099
02:22:20.940 --> 02:22:21.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, what we did was,

asr-003100
02:22:21.660 --> 02:22:24.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we consulted with the Department of Agriculture, World Food Program,

asr-003101
02:22:24.680 --> 02:22:26.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and we revamped it as early as 2023,

asr-003102
02:22:27.020 --> 02:22:28.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na isa, dalawa lang ang ginagawa nila,

asr-003103
02:22:28.580 --> 02:22:30.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: two monolithic programs nationwide.

asr-003104
02:22:30.980 --> 02:22:33.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's called LAWA, which are sweeps yun,

asr-003105
02:22:33.580 --> 02:22:36.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: yung small water impounding projects.

asr-003106
02:22:37.260 --> 02:22:39.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, we asked the A, where are the springs?

asr-003107
02:22:39.860 --> 02:22:42.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi doon namin nilalagay yung mga sweeps natin.

asr-003108
02:22:43.180 --> 02:22:44.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And then they would also plant around it.

asr-003109
02:22:45.020 --> 02:22:51.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, right now, these are found in communities that were targeted initially by the Climate Change Commission,

asr-003110
02:22:51.660 --> 02:22:53.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and pag-aasa as drought.

asr-003111
02:22:53.700 --> 02:22:59.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Noon pa, as drought, malapit sila sa drought, or any forms of climate change.

asr-003112
02:23:00.080 --> 02:23:05.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, these are the same communities that will be affected or are being affected already by El Nino.

asr-003113
02:23:05.040 --> 02:23:12.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, these sweeps or small water impounding systems na help them irrigate small community farms

asr-003114
02:23:12.080 --> 02:23:16.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and at the same time provide income because yung mga naaani nila dyan,

asr-003115
02:23:16.540 --> 02:23:21.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: by the way, yung seeds at yung mga isda na linalagay dyan ay galing sa PA.

asr-003116
02:23:21.660 --> 02:23:23.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sila nag-iprovide ng technical assistance.

asr-003117
02:23:24.100 --> 02:23:29.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Binibenta nila yan either through feeding program, through the Walang Gutom, or they consume it themselves.

asr-003118
02:23:29.920 --> 02:23:38.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, somehow, yung panawagan ng DA na to do community gardens to ease prices ng pagkain is already underway.

asr-003119
02:23:38.600 --> 02:23:41.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We, in fact, have 5,000 of these sweeps nationwide.

asr-003120
02:23:42.400 --> 02:23:44.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Small water impounding projects.

asr-003121
02:23:45.200 --> 02:23:46.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hindi ho yan nangyari overnight.

asr-003122
02:23:46.560 --> 02:23:50.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pinaghandaan ho namin siya since 2023, kaya ganyan karami ho yan.

asr-003123
02:23:50.120 --> 02:23:51.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These sweeps are still...

asr-003124
02:23:51.660 --> 02:23:52.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: active right now.

asr-003125
02:23:53.280 --> 02:23:59.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And the Department of Agriculture is helping us by introducing drought-resilient crops,

asr-003126
02:24:00.520 --> 02:24:07.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: both high-value and regular, katulad ng taro, kamote, and pag high-value, watermelon, okra.

asr-003127
02:24:07.540 --> 02:24:10.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, yan ho yung mga... yan yung partnership namin ng Department of Agriculture.

asr-003128
02:24:11.360 --> 02:24:15.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, when we say resilient, so kasi we didn't look at El Nino just now,

asr-003129
02:24:15.660 --> 02:24:20.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: but we were looking at El Nino way back in 2023, or La Nina as a matter of fact.

asr-003130
02:24:20.020 --> 02:24:21.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 5,000 small water...

asr-003131
02:24:21.660 --> 02:24:26.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: small water impounding systems or projects cannot be built in a span of couple of months.

asr-003132
02:24:26.800 --> 02:24:28.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That this was done way, way back.

asr-003133
02:24:28.840 --> 02:24:31.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, that's the first one in terms of social development.

asr-003134
02:24:31.240 --> 02:24:32.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We provide cash assistance.

asr-003135
02:24:32.480 --> 02:24:34.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: By the way, baka matanong nyo anong connection namin doon?

asr-003136
02:24:34.960 --> 02:24:38.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yung cash for work nila, for 20 days, they do the sweeps lang.

asr-003137
02:24:38.160 --> 02:24:39.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: They do the impounding lang.

asr-003138
02:24:39.800 --> 02:24:43.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And then, kung ano yung inani doon sa kanila na yun, and then napapaikot na nila by themselves.

asr-003139
02:24:44.480 --> 02:24:45.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, on the second slide...

asr-003140
02:24:46.740 --> 02:24:51.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The second slide, obviously, yung bilanggit ni Sekiko kanina,

asr-003141
02:24:51.220 --> 02:24:54.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: yung farmers na maapektuhan.

asr-003142
02:24:54.240 --> 02:25:00.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nag-start na ho kami ng emergency cash transfers in Cagayan, in Isabela, Camarines Norte, as we speak.

asr-003143
02:25:01.300 --> 02:25:05.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, we are monitoring it based on the declarations of state of calamity.

asr-003144
02:25:05.340 --> 02:25:10.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And like Sekiko said, may close coordination kami, they will pass on to us areas of vulnerability.

asr-003145
02:25:11.200 --> 02:25:16.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Na tulad ng nangyari sa RSSI, they were the ones who told us which provinces to move into

asr-003146
02:25:16.080 --> 02:25:17.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: based also on the state of calamity.

asr-003147
02:25:18.340 --> 02:25:18.820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Next slide.

asr-003148
02:25:20.440 --> 02:25:21.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, parang-parang...

asr-003149
02:25:21.220 --> 02:25:25.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For our social development, natatanong ho ito lagi sa akin, yung community-driven development o yung kalahi.

asr-003150
02:25:26.000 --> 02:25:31.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Remember, kalahi, naubos na ho yung ODA niyan when we joined the department in 2024.

asr-003151
02:25:31.760 --> 02:25:37.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, we applied for a new ODA that was approved, and you can see it in the unprogrammed also at my line item yan.

asr-003152
02:25:37.160 --> 02:25:38.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's called Pagkilos.

asr-003153
02:25:38.880 --> 02:25:43.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Basically, the community-driven development was converted into community-driven development

asr-003154
02:25:43.660 --> 02:25:46.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: looking at disaster resilience to include droughts.

asr-003155
02:25:46.900 --> 02:25:50.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, one particular project that already opened and we're expanding it will be...

asr-003156
02:25:51.220 --> 02:25:58.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, this community, for instance, in Masbate, nasa isla yan, I've been there, wala talagang tubig sila.

asr-003157
02:25:58.800 --> 02:26:06.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, this system is supposed to help them in the wash, to come up with sanitary water para sa mga community nila

asr-003158
02:26:06.620 --> 02:26:11.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kasi right now, they have to go to the town proper and spend so much money to get just a liter of water.

asr-003159
02:26:11.740 --> 02:26:14.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And right now, it's coming in handy during the El Nino.

asr-003160
02:26:15.020 --> 02:26:19.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, our approach, Madam Chairman, is both social development and social protection.

asr-003161
02:26:20.100 --> 02:26:21.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Social protection.

asr-003162
02:26:21.220 --> 02:26:25.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yung ECT as a means of bridging them para hindi ho sila mahulog palalim sa kahirapan.

asr-003163
02:26:26.440 --> 02:26:30.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: When we look at AICs or emergency cash transfer, hindi naman siya the ends to the means.

asr-003164
02:26:30.680 --> 02:26:31.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The means to the end.

asr-003165
02:26:31.940 --> 02:26:33.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But rather, it's a pantawid.

asr-003166
02:26:33.740 --> 02:26:40.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, sana gagamitin namin yun para maitawid sila, yung mga magsasaka o yung mga mangingisda na maapektuhan during the next six months.

asr-003167
02:26:40.520 --> 02:26:44.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero at the same time, we're embarking on social development programs that are meant for the long term.

asr-003168
02:26:45.000 --> 02:26:50.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Katulad ng Project Lawat Binhi at netong air-to-water system ng community-driven development.

asr-003169
02:26:51.220 --> 02:27:00.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung kaninang pinakita ninyo, can we go back to that slide?

asr-003170
02:27:00.340 --> 02:27:10.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung slide ng mga binigyan ng may different categories in uplift slide.

asr-003171
02:27:10.980 --> 02:27:15.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nakita ko na ang beneficiaries noon is about 6.5 million?

asr-003172
02:27:15.560 --> 02:27:16.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sir, sir.

asr-003173
02:27:16.940 --> 02:27:17.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 6.5 million.

asr-003174
02:27:17.640 --> 02:27:19.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes, but the target was 7.5.

asr-003175
02:27:19.840 --> 02:27:20.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Hinahanap pa namin.

asr-003176
02:27:20.720 --> 02:27:25.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Well, yan ay hinahanap namin using CPMSS data and SSS data.

asr-003177
02:27:25.520 --> 02:27:32.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But, and ang ginamit na pondo dyan is the IX fund, no?

asr-003178
02:27:32.040 --> 02:27:33.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The IX po ang ginagamit ko dyan.

asr-003179
02:27:33.620 --> 02:27:41.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then, dito sa slide ninyo, slide 11, nakita ko na to date or September, as of September,

asr-003180
02:27:41.960 --> 02:27:48.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ang beneficiaries is about, total beneficiaries is 8.7 million beneficiaries.

asr-003181
02:27:48.860 --> 02:27:49.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, in other words…

asr-003182
02:27:50.720 --> 02:27:58.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung uplift, andiyan pala, 8.7 million yung beneficiaries.

asr-003183
02:27:59.500 --> 02:28:03.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero, out of that 8.7, 7.5 galing sa…

asr-003184
02:28:03.780 --> 02:28:07.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: To clarify, Madam Chair, both are drawn from the IX funds.

asr-003185
02:28:08.320 --> 02:28:12.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Itong tinutukoy ng slide na to, na tinutukoy ng Senate President, ay IX regular.

asr-003186
02:28:13.180 --> 02:28:14.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ito ho yung mga pumupunta sa sasina.

asr-003187
02:28:14.280 --> 02:28:15.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero dyan rin kinuhin uplift?

asr-003188
02:28:15.580 --> 02:28:18.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes, kinukuha siya from the same pot.

asr-003189
02:28:18.720 --> 02:28:18.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-003190
02:28:19.100 --> 02:28:20.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang punto ko dito kasi…

asr-003191
02:28:20.720 --> 02:28:30.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang 2027 is 4.6 million ang target beneficiaries, or pwedeng mag-apply for the IX fund, di ba?

asr-003192
02:28:31.520 --> 02:28:37.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kung ang DA is already projecting at the worst case scenario, 4 million, ubos na kagad yan sa DA.

asr-003193
02:28:38.780 --> 02:28:40.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's a point I'm trying to make.

asr-003194
02:28:41.060 --> 02:28:42.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And this is only DA.

asr-003195
02:28:43.280 --> 02:28:50.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi pa natin kinakount yan kung tuloy-tuloy yung gera sa Iran at sumipa to $150 per barrel, or even $200.

asr-003196
02:28:50.720 --> 02:28:52.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi natin malaman ngayon.

asr-003197
02:28:52.840 --> 02:28:54.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Medyo wild-wild west doon.

asr-003198
02:28:55.020 --> 02:29:04.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, the 4 million is only for the farmers, pero we all learned na sa uplift, 7.5 ang binigyan na.

asr-003199
02:29:05.180 --> 02:29:07.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, mayroon pa tayong…

asr-003200
02:29:08.400 --> 02:29:17.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dapat ang nakahanda tayo is between 4 million to maybe 8 million beneficiaries for the next 6 to 12 months.

asr-003201
02:29:17.240 --> 02:29:20.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, yun ang nakikita kong based on the briefing ng mga sekretary.

asr-003202
02:29:20.420 --> 02:29:22.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, yun ang nakikita kong dapat paghandaan natin.

asr-003203
02:29:23.340 --> 02:29:28.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But 2027, in other words, is only 4.6.

asr-003204
02:29:28.660 --> 02:29:32.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, hindi siya responsive to the situation in the next 6 to 12 months.

asr-003205
02:29:32.480 --> 02:29:33.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Mabuti kung walang gera.

asr-003206
02:29:33.980 --> 02:29:36.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Mabuti kung walang El Nino, di ba?

asr-003207
02:29:36.680 --> 02:29:37.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Baka pwede yan.

asr-003208
02:29:37.700 --> 02:29:39.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In the normal circumstances, pwede yan.

asr-003209
02:29:39.860 --> 02:29:44.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero alam naman natin, in the next 6 to 12 months, ibang situation natin.

asr-003210
02:29:46.800 --> 02:29:48.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Very delikado yung ating situation.

asr-003211
02:29:48.680 --> 02:29:55.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But I'm sure that's why we have been very vocal about augmenting the AICs kasi it becomes our lifeline.

asr-003212
02:29:56.620 --> 02:29:59.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And rightfully so, as the Senate President pointed out, bagamat meron kaming…

asr-003213
02:29:59.840 --> 02:30:00.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ibang fund source

asr-003214
02:30:00.720 --> 02:30:02.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: like emergency cash transfer,

asr-003215
02:30:02.400 --> 02:30:03.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: it's really never enough.

asr-003216
02:30:04.020 --> 02:30:05.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And just to point out,

asr-003217
02:30:05.800 --> 02:30:06.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: umabot na rin ho kami

asr-003218
02:30:06.640 --> 02:30:07.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: sa punto ngayon

asr-003219
02:30:07.360 --> 02:30:08.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na humihingi na kami

asr-003220
02:30:08.220 --> 02:30:09.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ng fund augmentation

asr-003221
02:30:09.260 --> 02:30:10.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: from DBM

asr-003222
02:30:10.060 --> 02:30:12.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to beef up AICs

asr-003223
02:30:12.200 --> 02:30:14.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kasi nga hindi na siya sapat.

asr-003224
02:30:14.680 --> 02:30:15.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kasi we've spent

asr-003225
02:30:15.660 --> 02:30:16.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 10 billion immediately

asr-003226
02:30:16.660 --> 02:30:17.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: during the summer

asr-003227
02:30:17.380 --> 02:30:18.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for the transfer workers.

asr-003228
02:30:19.400 --> 02:30:20.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tapos ngayon,

asr-003229
02:30:20.120 --> 02:30:21.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we're supposed to cater

