03:46:52.800 --> 03:46:56.580
Dr. Liza Martinez: the implemented sections of the Magna Carta.

asr-005942
03:46:57.480 --> 03:47:01.060
Dr. Liza Martinez: And regarding particularly the auxiliary social services,

asr-005943
03:47:01.060 --> 03:47:11.240
Dr. Liza Martinez: and our good Secretary mentioned that they have already proposed indicators for the SGLC to compel LGUs to comply.

asr-005944
03:47:12.780 --> 03:47:16.620
Dr. Liza Martinez: And that has to do with my last point later on.

asr-005945
03:47:16.980 --> 03:47:18.220
Dr. Liza Martinez: And also our...

asr-005946
03:47:18.220 --> 03:47:19.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I thought your last point was now.

asr-005947
03:47:20.360 --> 03:47:20.880
Dr. Liza Martinez: Okay.

asr-005948
03:47:20.880 --> 03:47:21.680
Dr. Liza Martinez: Okay.

asr-005949
03:47:22.800 --> 03:47:35.300
Dr. Liza Martinez: N-C-D-A-E-D, Ms. Relova, and because we were asking even in the budget hearings of the House regarding Filipino Sign Language interpreters,

asr-005950
03:47:35.400 --> 03:47:46.940
Dr. Liza Martinez: and they mentioned an upcoming or ongoing DSWD Academy training allotted for 1 million four times a year, 45 trainees, and that you already have 80 interpreters on your roster.

asr-005951
03:47:47.460 --> 03:47:52.360
Dr. Liza Martinez: However, on the ground, we have received cases of rape victims.

asr-005952
03:47:52.360 --> 03:48:05.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: And they're usually women and girls who are unschooled and therefore much more vulnerable who have been advised by the social workers to learn sign language first on their own so that they could have the communication skills.

asr-005953
03:48:05.880 --> 03:48:08.200
Dr. Liza Martinez: Essentially, we feel this is highly discriminatory.

asr-005954
03:48:08.940 --> 03:48:21.140
Dr. Liza Martinez: And especially so since the Supreme Court has already issued a rule on interpreting, specifically institutionalizing deaf-rely interpreters for unschooled deaf people.

asr-005955
03:48:21.560 --> 03:48:22.240
Dr. Liza Martinez: So,

asr-005956
03:48:22.360 --> 03:48:28.520
Dr. Liza Martinez: they may not sign in the standard language, but they are highly communicative.

asr-005957
03:48:29.240 --> 03:48:37.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: So, we are very disturbed because the incidence of rape and sexual violence is about 10 times higher than the national average.

asr-005958
03:48:37.340 --> 03:48:38.620
Dr. Liza Martinez: Last 30 seconds.

asr-005959
03:48:41.540 --> 03:48:42.520
Dr. Liza Martinez: Last na po.

asr-005960
03:48:42.720 --> 03:48:46.640
Dr. Liza Martinez: Here is just a challenge or food for thought.

asr-005961
03:48:47.660 --> 03:48:51.180
Dr. Liza Martinez: We have been talking a lot since Monday about the PWD IDs.

asr-005962
03:48:51.180 --> 03:49:09.220
Dr. Liza Martinez: Maybe it is time for us to step back a little and maybe not put too much value on the discounts and the VAT exemption if we can provide a whole of government approach in really providing services to persons with disabilities.

asr-005963
03:49:09.220 --> 03:49:20.520
Dr. Liza Martinez: I can imagine that if there is no discount, then the government will have all agencies, not just DSWD na sila ang tinuturo lagi or DILG only.

asr-005964
03:49:20.520 --> 03:49:25.560
Dr. Liza Martinez: But all agencies have to provide, make their public services accessible to all.

asr-005965
03:49:26.500 --> 03:49:34.200
Dr. Liza Martinez: The reason that disability is such a beast to deal with siguro in governance, it's because it's a highly diverse group.

asr-005966
03:49:35.200 --> 03:49:48.060
Dr. Liza Martinez: You're talking about, we have many conceptions of sino ba yung totoong person with a disability and laking debate niyan between the SWDD or HNCDA and so on.

asr-005967
03:49:48.060 --> 03:49:49.760
Dr. Liza Martinez: Where are the deaf-blind?

asr-005968
03:49:49.760 --> 03:50:02.820
Dr. Liza Martinez: Where are, we don't talk very often about those on the spectrum, those with intellectual disabilities, and those with mental health, those who have episodic and chronic conditions.

asr-005969
03:50:02.920 --> 03:50:03.640
Dr. Liza Martinez: You don't see them.

asr-005970
03:50:04.880 --> 03:50:06.660
Dr. Liza Martinez: And sometimes they're all just lumped.

asr-005971
03:50:06.760 --> 03:50:08.000
Dr. Liza Martinez: O, psychosocial kayo lahat.

asr-005972
03:50:09.060 --> 03:50:09.700
Dr. Liza Martinez: Okay.

asr-005973
03:50:10.120 --> 03:50:17.320
Dr. Liza Martinez: And our experience with the deaf, it shows that this whole government approach is so critical.

asr-005974
03:50:17.320 --> 03:50:19.260
Dr. Liza Martinez: And this is our appeal to the committee.

asr-005975
03:50:19.760 --> 03:50:22.620
Dr. Liza Martinez: Let us not just put it all on one agency.

asr-005976
03:50:23.320 --> 03:50:33.840
Dr. Liza Martinez: Because for instance, if we look at the 2,000 proposed disability support allowance, 2,000 per month, one interpreting for one hour is already 1,000.

asr-005977
03:50:34.500 --> 03:50:38.380
Dr. Liza Martinez: Going to see a developmental pediatrician is at least 5,000.

asr-005978
03:50:39.020 --> 03:50:48.820
Dr. Liza Martinez: Taking a grab, just to go from if you're in a wheelchair or you have to carry your child who has severe cerebral palsy,

asr-005979
03:50:48.820 --> 03:50:51.180
Dr. Liza Martinez: will take you at least 800 pesos.

asr-005980
03:50:51.500 --> 03:50:52.920
Dr. Liza Martinez: Wala ka agad yung 2,000.

asr-005981
03:50:57.360 --> 03:51:05.600
Dr. Liza Martinez: There are now 35 deaf people who have been arrested without being read their rights.

asr-005982
03:51:05.780 --> 03:51:08.800
Dr. Liza Martinez: They do not know why they're being arrested.

asr-005983
03:51:09.720 --> 03:51:13.700
Dr. Liza Martinez: There was an attempt to translate the Miranda rights,

asr-005984
03:51:13.700 --> 03:51:17.740
Dr. Liza Martinez: but it was done, unfortunately, without the lack of awareness.

asr-005985
03:51:17.860 --> 03:51:18.700
Dr. Liza Martinez: That you have to ask deaf people.

asr-005986
03:51:18.820 --> 03:51:21.080
Dr. Liza Martinez: So that they can be understood.

asr-005987
03:51:21.260 --> 03:51:23.760
Dr. Liza Martinez: These are mostly deaf people who have never been to school.

asr-005988
03:51:24.780 --> 03:51:26.380
Dr. Liza Martinez: The number is growing.

asr-005989
03:51:27.360 --> 03:51:31.080
Dr. Liza Martinez: Where are we in the deaf-deaf SDGs?

asr-005990
03:51:31.980 --> 03:51:34.360
Dr. Liza Martinez: The time will be up in three years.

asr-005991
03:51:34.500 --> 03:51:41.260
Dr. Liza Martinez: We have had 15 years, SDG 1 on the poverty about leaving no one behind.

asr-005992
03:51:42.560 --> 03:51:45.440
Dr. Liza Martinez: Persons with disabilities and children are already left behind.

asr-005993
03:51:45.500 --> 03:51:48.180
Dr. Liza Martinez: Because there's no data even up until now.

asr-005994
03:51:48.820 --> 03:51:54.660
Dr. Liza Martinez: How much is government spending for persons with disabilities, including children with disabilities?

asr-005995
03:51:54.660 --> 03:52:01.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: The only study which has been done was in 2013 by Civil Society, the Philippine Coalition on the CRPD.

asr-005996
03:52:01.160 --> 03:52:03.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: But as of now, we don't know.

asr-005997
03:52:03.160 --> 03:52:05.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: We are invisible.

asr-005998
03:52:05.160 --> 03:52:07.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: Okay, this is the final.

asr-005999
03:52:07.160 --> 03:52:11.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, please, because also Senator Amy would actually like to interject here.

asr-006000
03:52:11.160 --> 03:52:13.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay, so please wrap up, Ms. Liza.

asr-006001
03:52:13.160 --> 03:52:17.860
Dr. Liza Martinez: This is a provision which builds on, this is for the deaf,

asr-006002
03:52:17.860 --> 03:52:23.080
Dr. Liza Martinez: and the main point, it has several things, we have sent the draft,

asr-006003
03:52:23.900 --> 03:52:27.380
Dr. Liza Martinez: is to make persons with disabilities visible.

asr-006004
03:52:28.100 --> 03:52:34.340
Dr. Liza Martinez: We are not asking for any appropriation, but we are asking for certain accounting,

asr-006005
03:52:34.780 --> 03:52:39.140
Dr. Liza Martinez: you know, governance mechanisms, just so that it can be seen.

asr-006006
03:52:39.260 --> 03:52:42.160
Dr. Liza Martinez: Because if you're out of sight, you're out of mind.

asr-006007
03:52:42.460 --> 03:52:43.280
Dr. Liza Martinez: That's all. Thank you very much.

asr-006008
03:52:43.760 --> 03:52:44.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-006009
03:52:44.280 --> 03:52:45.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you very much, Ms. Liza.

asr-006010
03:52:45.580 --> 03:52:47.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, for the Chair.

asr-006011
03:52:47.300 --> 03:52:47.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Senator, I'm...

asr-006012
03:52:47.860 --> 03:52:57.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dr. Martinez's plea that, in fact, those with severe challenges should actually be provided their own stipend.

asr-006013
03:52:57.900 --> 03:53:06.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I filed in the last Congress still a disability support fund already and refiled it in 2025 last year.

asr-006014
03:53:07.260 --> 03:53:08.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: But we had discussions.

asr-006015
03:53:09.040 --> 03:53:14.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It's a far more modest proposition at 500 bucks per month, which is hardly enough, as you said,

asr-006016
03:53:14.900 --> 03:53:17.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: because it's extremely expensive, assistive devices.

asr-006017
03:53:17.860 --> 03:53:21.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Therapy, et cetera, is already quite onerous.

asr-006018
03:53:21.460 --> 03:53:28.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And we came to some kind of agreement at that point in time, sa 500 a month lang muna.

asr-006019
03:53:28.440 --> 03:53:31.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi kailangan mag-identify ka ng funding source.

asr-006020
03:53:31.740 --> 03:53:32.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi ba, alam ni Chair yun.

asr-006021
03:53:33.660 --> 03:53:38.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At sana mabuhay ngayon, and I appreciate hearing it from you,

asr-006022
03:53:38.200 --> 03:53:40.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: because nanahimik na yung bilis.

asr-006023
03:53:40.700 --> 03:53:42.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sana buhayin natin ulit.

asr-006024
03:53:42.460 --> 03:53:46.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At tigit sa lahat, very alarming nga ang criminal statistics,

asr-006025
03:53:46.460 --> 03:53:47.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: yung mga crimes against chastity.

asr-006026
03:53:47.860 --> 03:53:52.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And sexual assault sa ating deaf community.

asr-006027
03:53:53.120 --> 03:53:54.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And also the blind community.

asr-006028
03:53:55.020 --> 03:53:56.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Talagang malaking problema yan.

asr-006029
03:53:57.320 --> 03:54:01.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At kinakailangan talaga pagtuunan ng pansin.

asr-006030
03:54:01.440 --> 03:54:04.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero in the SWD, severely hampered, as are the LGUs,

asr-006031
03:54:05.260 --> 03:54:12.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: for lack na nga of the psychologists, psychiatrists, and others who can identify mental

asr-006032
03:54:12.640 --> 03:54:17.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and the cover, catch-all, psychosocial neurodivergence,

asr-006033
03:54:17.860 --> 03:54:19.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: divergent, etc., classification.

asr-006034
03:54:21.160 --> 03:54:21.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Sen. Amy.

asr-006035
03:54:22.080 --> 03:54:29.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Before I ask the Secretary if he'd like to respond initially dun sa inputs ni Ms. Liza,

asr-006036
03:54:29.640 --> 03:54:37.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: gusto kong i-confirm na meron nga ang mga disability support allowances bills filed.

asr-006037
03:54:38.460 --> 03:54:44.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung sa representasyong ito, 2,000 a month din ang proposal sa bill.

asr-006038
03:54:44.320 --> 03:54:46.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, pagtutulungan na lang namin i-follow up.

asr-006039
03:54:47.240 --> 03:54:47.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Muli.

asr-006040
03:54:47.520 --> 03:54:51.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Muli itong kongreso yung proposals namin iyon.

asr-006041
03:54:52.240 --> 03:54:57.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ang ganda po nung proposal about a predictable rights-based social protection.

asr-006042
03:54:58.700 --> 03:55:05.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And sinare ko rin kay Secrex nung mga briefings namin na gusto ko talaga ma-raise yung profile ng department

asr-006043
03:55:05.580 --> 03:55:15.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: aside from for their essential, urgent, tactical responses, yung long-term strategic trajectory ng department.

asr-006044
03:55:15.080 --> 03:55:17.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And I think isang magandang possible anchor ito.

asr-006045
03:55:17.520 --> 03:55:22.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung rights-based social protection na ang DSWD ang mag-champion yan.

asr-006046
03:55:22.700 --> 03:55:32.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, well-noted yung mga specific proposed, possible proposed amendments for 2027 na i-restore to at least 2026 levels

asr-006047
03:55:32.920 --> 03:55:35.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at o i-adopt yung Tier 2.

asr-006048
03:55:35.540 --> 03:55:40.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then yung possible amendment on the child protection system.

asr-006049
03:55:42.400 --> 03:55:47.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kaugnay din ito sa kapapasa din naming batang ligtas.

asr-006050
03:55:47.520 --> 03:55:48.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Law, no?

asr-006051
03:55:48.140 --> 03:55:51.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Laban nga sa OSAIC, CISAEM, at pati laban sa NVE.

asr-006052
03:55:51.700 --> 03:55:54.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then yun na nga po yung disability support allowance.

asr-006053
03:55:54.800 --> 03:55:56.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, Secrex, would you like to respond?

asr-006054
03:55:56.700 --> 03:55:58.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Well-noted, Madam Chair.

asr-006055
03:55:58.840 --> 03:56:07.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Actually, Social Watch Philippines is a partner of ours in the cabinet cluster on social development and social protection.

asr-006056
03:56:08.120 --> 03:56:10.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, all the points that they raise are well-noted.

asr-006057
03:56:10.340 --> 03:56:17.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: I just want to put on record na meron na ho tayong mga incubator social protection programs in those areas.

asr-006058
03:56:17.520 --> 03:56:18.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At least that you mentioned.

asr-006059
03:56:19.160 --> 03:56:24.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: First of all is yung binalik sa house na budget na 25 million for Project Aruga.

asr-006060
03:56:24.980 --> 03:56:32.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Project Aruga is a pilot project that takes care of the family, the caregivers themselves, as well as the child na may disability.

asr-006061
03:56:32.800 --> 03:56:36.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, it calls for support in early detection, assessments.

asr-006062
03:56:37.620 --> 03:56:40.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Number two, meron ng disability support allowance na TIG to 2,000.

asr-006063
03:56:41.440 --> 03:56:43.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And then they also get auxiliary services.

asr-006064
03:56:43.620 --> 03:56:47.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're going to use our AICs to tie up with service providers in the area.

asr-006065
03:56:47.520 --> 03:56:53.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So that whatever therapy or whatever intervention that they need, especially for children with special needs,

asr-006066
03:56:54.240 --> 03:56:59.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: can seek help using our guarantee letters ng AICs program, another use of the AICs program.

asr-006067
03:57:00.540 --> 03:57:06.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And then it also calls for, it also has a built-in capacity building for family support

asr-006068
03:57:06.000 --> 03:57:11.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: because it can be taxing for the family of a person with disability on how to cope.

asr-006069
03:57:12.260 --> 03:57:14.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We also have to take care of the family themselves.

asr-006070
03:57:14.400 --> 03:57:16.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And last, advocacy campaigns.

asr-006071
03:57:17.520 --> 03:57:20.820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: A lot of people are still ignorant, not because they choose to do so,

asr-006072
03:57:20.900 --> 03:57:24.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: but because of lack of information on what they should and not do,

asr-006073
03:57:24.580 --> 03:57:26.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: what they should say and what not say,

asr-006074
03:57:26.640 --> 03:57:29.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or how they should refer to people with disabilities.

asr-006075
03:57:29.560 --> 03:57:31.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, the whole program is holistic.

asr-006076
03:57:31.520 --> 03:57:33.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sa HGAB po, nabalik na ho siya, 25 million.

asr-006077
03:57:34.460 --> 03:57:36.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Malit lang ho siya, but it's a good starting point.

asr-006078
03:57:37.080 --> 03:57:41.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These are pilot programs in selected LGUs that we can learn from

asr-006079
03:57:41.960 --> 03:57:45.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: so that pagka time na may budget na mas malaki,

asr-006080
03:57:45.520 --> 03:57:47.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we can already have the learnings and the impact.

asr-006081
03:57:47.520 --> 03:57:49.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The assessments and the monitorings.

asr-006082
03:57:49.920 --> 03:57:56.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pangalawa po, the other fund that was restored was the 25 million fund for Project SAFE,

asr-006083
03:57:56.140 --> 03:57:58.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: which is an OSAIC advocacy campaign.

asr-006084
03:57:59.080 --> 03:58:04.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: One, it teaches people or the young people on what to look out for in their families,

asr-006085
03:58:04.860 --> 03:58:05.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the red flags.

asr-006086
03:58:06.160 --> 03:58:11.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pangalawa, it has a strong reporting system and network of care for OSAIC victims.

asr-006087
03:58:12.540 --> 03:58:17.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pangatlo, obviously what we do best are healing services in our care facilities.

asr-006088
03:58:17.520 --> 03:58:21.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And pangapat, recovery and reintegration services.

asr-006089
03:58:22.160 --> 03:58:25.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, it's again a pilot because of the tight fiscal space,

asr-006090
03:58:25.100 --> 03:58:27.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: but at least nandun na ho siya, the 25 million.

asr-006091
03:58:27.820 --> 03:58:35.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, I totally agree with the good professor on restoring sana the attached agency budgets

asr-006092
03:58:35.060 --> 03:58:37.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: because these are administrative in nature.

asr-006093
03:58:37.520 --> 03:58:39.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: As mentioned to the good chairwoman,

asr-006094
03:58:39.820 --> 03:58:45.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: marami ho doon are employee-based na compensation na maaring mawala by next year

asr-006095
03:58:45.960 --> 03:58:47.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: kung hindi ho maibabalik yung mga points.

asr-006096
03:58:47.520 --> 03:58:53.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, we can do a better job with the implementation of FSL.

asr-006097
03:58:54.260 --> 03:58:56.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We admit that, we admitted that in the House.

asr-006098
03:58:58.060 --> 03:59:01.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kaming nga mismo sa Departamento, kulang ho kami.

asr-006099
03:59:01.780 --> 03:59:05.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, what is the concrete step towards the direction that you want?

asr-006100
03:59:05.460 --> 03:59:06.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Department has an academy.

asr-006101
03:59:06.920 --> 03:59:08.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's about to be opened by the end of the year.

asr-006102
03:59:08.880 --> 03:59:10.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Of course, we're running it off-site now.

asr-006103
03:59:11.360 --> 03:59:14.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The academy will work with the Philippine Association of the Deaf

asr-006104
03:59:14.260 --> 03:59:17.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to help capacitate our own service providers.

asr-006105
03:59:17.520 --> 03:59:19.880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: As well as LGU service providers

asr-006106
03:59:19.880 --> 03:59:23.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: by doing these courses inside our academy, these certification programs.

asr-006107
03:59:25.440 --> 03:59:28.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung kami nga ho mismo, like I said, we can do a better job,

asr-006108
03:59:28.380 --> 03:59:30.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: then admittedly, we should be doing a better job.

asr-006109
03:59:32.800 --> 03:59:33.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Secrex.

asr-006110
03:59:34.200 --> 03:59:36.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Can I just wrap up, Madam Chair?

asr-006111
03:59:36.960 --> 03:59:37.360
